{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/android/debug_keystore.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328799Z","id":"50df1c587bf774a97810a5076c7799fef0cfa586f3a8c4a45e5eed0011baa319","body":{"detail":"As apps/clax_app/android/app/build.gradle.kts signs its release build with the debug key, so an APK built by either installs over one already on the owner's phone (same certificate SHA-256 9874f8473ebc181beb90c6af8b4d29dfac87a97bcde62da0880a71938d28ce85 for the Gradle-built and the Bazel-built APK, 2026-10-17, apksigner verify --print-certs). The repository rule is local and watches the file; the APK targets are no-remote. Without the file (CI) rules_android's own key signs, and that APK does not install over a developer's. Accepted until the app has a release key.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"59247bf5fac45ba00942e592f3384bc8473401becee37f251b0e8dc1841627c3"},"summary":"The APK is signed with this machine's ~/.android/debug.keystore, an input Bazel does not pin","tags":["apk","signing","revisit:the app gets a release signing key","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
